      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "At least make this off by default. Users should be responsible for their own backups unless they opt in to it. I couldn't figure out why my upload speeds were so slow for months until someone told me to turn it off.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-06T17:29:04.126Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's on by default, but in reality it shouldn't exist.\n\nIt is common knowledge among many VRChat fan communities with creators that the future proofing feature is more of a detriment.\n\n- It uploads a full unity package of your avatar, which makes it then easier to steal by malicious users.\n- It makes your avatar uploading many times slower. I have a friend who makes worlds, and having it on turns a 2 minute world upload to a 30 minute world upload.\n- There is no usage case of this \"future proofing\" actually doing anything for us. Especially with the 2017 update, where literally nothing was future proof and some avatars had to be repaired or reuploaded.\n\nPeople should instead be vocally encouraged to save proper backups of their avatars and adopt a different workflow akin to what real developers do.\n\nIn my case, I backup all my projects via git to bitbucket, as it's nice to use commits as a quick way to keep an updated backup on my work.",
